 "tier_window": "0 fired windows outside send time + the tier horizon in every class and tier; free/basic/premium all resolve to 72 h (ALERTS_FORECAST_HORIZON_H 72 <= free's 3 days), so tier never binds at the default",
 "reason": "The replay is sane (perfect-forecast control precision 1.000, recall 0.95-0.97; at sigma 1 precision 0.457-0.731 vs today's simulated 0.031-0.281, recall 0.93-0.96, 0.36-1.46 alerts per user-day vs today's simulated ~15-23), but the brief's volume rule fails: the broad size-only class gets 4-5 alerts in one local day on 30 of 645 user-days (4.7%) at sigma 1 and up to 6 at sigma 2. The perfect-forecast control never exceeds 3, so the excess is forecast noise fragmenting one window into several non-overlapping ones that each re-announce.",
 "fix": "Add a per-user daily send cap (e.g. ALERTS_MAX_PER_USER_DAY 2-3) or suppress a new window that starts on the same local day as one already sent for that alert, then re-run this replay (target: max <= 3/user/day at sigma 1 and 2, precision not lower). Also: if Render env carries ALERTS_FORECAST_WINDOWS='0' explicitly, a code-default flip alone will not turn the scheduler on (env change is the owner's).",
 "reaches_users": "YES - push notifications",
